# core.autocrlf is on for this machine, and git guesses that the press kit PDF
# is text because its first bytes are ASCII. That means checkout rewrites LF to
# CRLF inside the file and hands back a PDF hundreds of bytes larger than the
# one that was committed. Mark the binaries so git leaves their bytes alone.

*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
